index 7d73637..b1036c7 100644
--- a/docs/subsystems/agent-wiring.md
+++ b/docs/subsystems/agent-wiring.md
@@ -244,3 +244,8 @@ Settings included, so the form, the saved row and gateway traffic have not
 been tried end to end. As with Cindy and Lody, the TUI leaves the row out
 because there is nothing to pick. `magpie aionui add` opens the link.
 
+## Augma native assistant
+
+[`augma.go`](../../internal/agent/augma.go) detects the macOS app after its first launch exports `~/Library/Application Support/Augma/Assistant/magpie.json`. Schema version 1 holds `runtime`, `model`, `effort` and an optional `managed` flag. Connecting stashes these four keys, chooses DSH, and writes the catalog model and a supported effort. Unknown fields remain. Disconnect restores the original keys; unreadable or unsupported files are never overwritten. The agent exposes only the intersection of the catalog efforts and the installed Augma/DSH supported levels (through max, excluding ultra).
+
+Augma imports the file on activation and before a model request. A changed selection cancels the old runtime and invalidates its connection test; the user tests and enables it in Augma. The file cannot grant tools, enable sending, change the DSH executable, or contain credentials. Augma discovers the local gateway separately; the DSH desktop profile is not modified. There is no gateway-address `Check` hook: this adapter manages selections, while DSH manages its route. `TestAugmaRegistrationAndDetection`, `TestAugmaModelEffortAndDisconnect` and `TestAugmaRejectsInvalidConfigAndUnknownModel` cover registration, selections, restoration and refusal. `TestAugmaConnectKeepsExistingGroup` checks that first connect preserves the full named group ID through `Join`, before generic matching strips provider prefixes.
